{
  "name": "Eschaton Foundry",
  "icon": "theoreticalsciences:eschaton_foundry",
  "category": "theoreticalsciences:endgame",
  "sortnum": 91,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:eschaton_foundry",
      "title": "Eschaton Foundry",
      "text": "A sphere of Pleroma glass on a waist of Omnipotence casing, ringed in Logos coil and watched by four towers. It packs as much as the laws allow into as little space as they allow - right up to the edge of becoming a black hole - and repeats what you once forged by hand.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 5$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "This controller is too complex for a crafting grid. Build it on the $(item)Femtoscale Assembly Line$() - check JEI for the exact parts."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Makes the $(item)Absolute Singularity$(), the $(item)Echo of the Transcendental$(), $(item)Eschaton Cells$() and the $(item)Eschaton Core$() - but only what its owner has forged by hand in the Core's Forge at least once. It costs far more than the Forge, and it never has to wait."
    },
